IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-types`

-- Electricity Industry Act 2010 — GOAL 2: DISPUTES.
--
--   "May this person complain to the dispute resolution scheme about this
--    participant, and must the participant be a member?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_2010_116.txt — ss 95-96.

§ `Goal 2 — disputes`

-- s 95 "(1) Any person described in subsection (2) may make a complaint to the
-- dispute resolution scheme concerning Transpower (except in its capacity as
-- system operator) or any distributor or retailer. (2) The persons who may
-- make a complaint are any persons ... except members of the dispute
-- resolution scheme."
@ref s 95(1)-(2)
GIVEN about IS A `Kind of participant`, complainantIsMember IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a complaint may be made about` about `, by a scheme member` complainantIsMember IF
        NOT complainantIsMember
    AND (   about EQUALS `Transpower, other than as system operator`
         OR about EQUALS `a distributor`
         OR about EQUALS `a retailer`)

-- s 96 "(1) Transpower (other than in its capacity as system operator), and
-- every distributor and retailer, must be a member of the dispute resolution
-- scheme, unless exempt under subsection (3). (2) A person commits an offence
-- and is liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $100,000 if the person
-- knowingly refuses or fails to become a member ... (3) A person need not be
-- a member ... if— (a) the person is a member of a class ... identified in
-- regulations ...; or (b) the Minister of Consumer Affairs exempts the person
-- by ... notice in the Gazette".
@ref s 96(1)-(3)
@export Whether a participant must be a member of the electricity dispute resolution scheme under s 96 of the Electricity Industry Act 2010 (NZ): Transpower (other than as system operator), every distributor and every retailer, unless in an exempt class or individually exempted by Gazette notice. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN s IS A `Scheme facts`  @desc The kind of participant and any class or individual exemption
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `must be a member of the dispute resolution scheme` s IF
        (   s's `kind of participant` EQUALS `Transpower, other than as system operator`
         OR s's `kind of participant` EQUALS `a distributor`
         OR s's `kind of participant` EQUALS `a retailer`)
    AND NOT s's `in an exempt class under regulations`
    AND NOT s's `individually exempted by Gazette notice`

@ref s 96(2)
GIVEN s IS A `Scheme facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most fine for not joining the scheme` s MEANS
    IF   `must be a member of the dispute resolution scheme` s AND (NOT s's `a member of the scheme`) AND s's `knowingly refused or failed to become a member`
    THEN 100000
    ELSE 0
